# Autopilot queue policy (Codimension)

When the user says `autopilot` / `/autopilot` / `.autopilot`:

1. Do **not** ask which PR or task to pick.
2. Resolve the work queue in this order:
   - [TODO_FIXME.md](TODO_FIXME.md) — first 🔓 OPEN or PARTIAL row (P0 before P1 before P2)
   - If TODO has no open rows, [ROADMAP.uk.md](ROADMAP.uk.md) / [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) — first **OPEN** atomic task (`Rxxx`)
3. Implement that item on a feature branch, open a PR to `sesquicadaver/codimension`, drive CI green.
4. After green CI + clean review of this cycle’s changes: commit/push as needed, then **merge the PR yourself** (standing order 2026-08-06). Do not leave merge to the user; babysit-only skills do not override this.
5. Update TODO_FIXME (if used) + Living Spec + ChangeLog + mark the ROADMAP row `DONE` with PR/SHA.

Current pointer: **active queue empty** (R179 done — PR #89). TODO_FIXME has no remaining 🔓 OPEN rows.
Deferred only (do not pull forward without an explicit ask): **R180**, **R181**, **R182**.
Active queue lists OPEN only; DONE history lives in ROADMAP Archive.
